@lrf=1|aud=LLM|scope=research
R|research.incident|task:local-incident|MUST|RO_LOCAL|target=localhost-or-private-host-incident; skip=pre-planning-web-and-epub; action=inspect-local-evidence-directly; search-memory=optional-for-prior-incident; external-search=on-demand-when-local-evidence-exhausted
R|research.order|*|MUST|RO_LOCAL|at task start run Get-Date -Format o; derive compact task keywords; local/private incident or local-rule consistency=>inspect local evidence first and mark public/EPUB sources N_A when inapplicable; otherwise web-first and EPUB if outdated/shallow/insufficient; reuse current-task PRECEDENT memory search; do not repeat on ordinary turns
R|research.retry-trigger|*|MUST|RO_LOCAL|rerun delegated exploration only after two distinct research or downstream validation failures; the second failure is the trigger, not the first; reset the counter after a successful pass
R|research.delegate|*|MUST|RO_LOCAL|apply agent.mode first; when Codex delegation is permitted and useful for independent workstreams or ambiguity, select Researcher with tag:subagent; otherwise main performs exploration directly; prohibition is an intentional local route, not a failed subagent run
R|research.delegate-model|*|MUST|RO_LOCAL|when delegation is permitted select Researcher through SUBAGENTS.lrf; routine=Codex Terra medium; ambiguous/high-impact=Codex Sol high or xhigh; never Astra; agy coding requirement does not force external research
R|research.delegate-output|*|MUST|RO_LOCAL|require minimal Researcher output sections Facts, Inferences, Unknowns, Sources, Precedents, Constraints, FAILED, ADVICE, and ESCALATE; main agent independently checks citations and separates fact from inference
R|research.delegate-fallback|*|MUST|RO_LOCAL|if a permitted Researcher run cannot execute, main performs applicable research.order steps directly and records FAILED for the attempted run; when prohibited use main directly without an invocation; never silently skip applicable research gates
R|research.web|*|MUST|RO_PUBLIC|use chrome-cdp-search or native web search with date-bounded keywords; prefer current primary sources; record source title, URL, publication date, accessed date, fact, inference, and unknown; if no public source applies record N_A with reason
R|research.epub|*|MUST|RO_LOCAL|condition=web-outdated-or-insufficient-or-offline; use rg.exe to locate kavita-fetch-search.exe; search Kavita metadata with search <keywords>; for candidate series run query <series_id> <keywords>; use EPUB hits only as fact-check evidence and record no-hit or unavailable explicitly; if web was sufficient record SKIPPED_CURRENT_WEB_SUFFICIENT
R|research.memory|*|MUST|RO_LOCAL|search llm-mem.exe for prior cases using compact task keywords with -level 2 -json; distinguish precedent from current fact; record no-hit or unavailable explicitly
R|research.synthesis|*|MUST|RO_LOCAL|after all checks present Facts, Inferences, Unknowns, Sources, Precedents, and Constraints before proposing implementation; never treat an inference as a verified fact
R|research.local-review|case:local-review|MUST|RO_LOCAL|bounded target search -> evidence -> targeted document diff check; collector facts are evidence only and the in-conversation report separates Facts, Inferences, and Unknowns
R|research.local-review-boundary|case:local-review|MUST|RO_LOCAL|edit/code/config/schema/public/external/live/VCS/credential/scope expansion -> normal gates; unknown/conflict/malformed/retry -> STOP; discovery outside the fixed target set -> handoff and End
R|research.local-review-commands|case:local-review|MUST|RO_LOCAL|collector may invoke only rg.exe fixed-string query, git status --short -- exact targets, and git diff --check -- exact targets; collector creates no memory/diary artifacts and executes no arbitrary commands; main runs mandatory mem.etl separately at FINISH
R|research.failure|*|MUST|RO_LOCAL|if a required search tool fails, report the exact non-secret failure and continue with available sources; do not silently skip the gate or fabricate results
R|research.secrets|*|MUST_NOT|CRED|never print or persist API keys, tokens, passwords, connection strings, private environment values, Kavita configuration, or raw credential-bearing output
